  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The scale was validated using data from a single, highly mature smart destination, which may limit its immediate generalizability to cities in earlier stages of smart development.",
      "what": "The study develops and validates the Smart Destination Perception Scale (SDPS), a 29-item instrument measuring how tourists and residents perceive smart cities. Using survey data from 1,200 participants in Madrid (split equally between 600 residents and 600 tourists), exploratory and confirmatory factor analyses identified four core dimensions: Innovation, Connectivity, Market Intelligence, and Social and Environmental Responsibility.",
      "why": "It provides a standardized, validated tool that allows municipal authorities to directly compare smart city performance across different destinations while simultaneously capturing the distinct viewpoints of both visitors and local inhabitants."
    }
